-- title:
--   Generic Frobenius of a p-th-power endomorphism of the fibre
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a nonzero $M$ with $p \mid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, and the hypothesis `hj` that the $q$-expansion $j(q)$ `jqModC ℚ` lies in the field $F =$ `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤` generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by ratios of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a nonunit of $A$, whose residue field $\kappa$ has characteristic $p$ and is algebraically closed, and let $\rho :$ `R p` $\to A$ be a ring map whose composite with the inclusion $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is the structure map; $\kappa$ is an `R p`-algebra via `residue ∘ ρ`. Let $M_{\mathrm{fib}}$ be a `CurveModel` over $\kappa$ with function field identified, by a ring isomorphism $\mathrm{ff} =$ `Mfib.ffEquiv`, with `qExpFunctionFieldC κ (ΓN p M H hpM)`: so $M_{\mathrm{fib}}.C$ is integral, proper and smooth of relative dimension $1$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\kappa$, with closed points in bijection with places. Let `efib` be an isomorphism from $M_{\mathrm{fib}}.C$ onto the fibre, i.e. the pullback of the two-chart integral model `toBase p (ΓN p M H hpM) hj` along $\operatorname{Spec}\kappa \to \operatorname{Spec}$ `R p`, compatible with the structure morphisms (`hefib`), whose preimage of the $j$-finite chart open `ιFin ''ᵁ ⊤` is nonempty. Assume the pinning hypothesis `Mfib_pin`: for every $b$ in the $j$-finite chart algebra `chartAlgFin p (ΓN p M H hpM) hj` (the elements of `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (ΓN p M H hpM)` integral over the `R p`-subalgebra generated by $j$) and every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose image in `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` is the $q$-expansion of $b$, the function-field element obtained by reading $b$ as a section on that chart open, taking its germ at the generic point and transporting it by $\mathrm{ff}^{-1}$, has $q$-expansion equal to the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $\theta$ be an endomorphism of the fibre over $\operatorname{Spec}\kappa$. Then, for every morphism $c_0 : \operatorname{Spec}(\kappa \otimes_{\mathrm{R}\,p}$ `chartAlgFin` $)$ to the fibre whose two components are $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the right inclusion followed by the chart immersion `ιFin`, respectively $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the left inclusion, and every $\kappa$-algebra endomorphism $\varphi$ of $\kappa \otimes_{\mathrm{R}\,p}$ `chartAlgFin` with $\varphi(1 \otimes b) = (1 \otimes b)^p$ for all chart elements $b$ and with $c_0$ followed by $\theta$ equal to $\operatorname{Spec}\varphi$ followed by $c_0$, the canonical morphism $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the stalk at the generic point of $M_{\mathrm{fib}}.C$, followed by the transported endomorphism `efib ≫ θ ≫ inv efib`, coincides with $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the conjugate $\mathrm{ff} \circ$ `qExpFrobeniusModL κ (ΓN p M H hpM) p` $\circ\, \mathrm{ff}^{-1}$ followed by that same canonical morphism, where `qExpFrobeniusModL` is the $\kappa$-algebra endomorphism $x(q) \mapsto x(q^p)$ of the $q$-expansion function field.
--
--   This identifies the behaviour at the generic point of an endomorphism of the mod-$p$ fibre of the two-chart integral model of the modular curve of level `ΓN p M H hpM` which acts as the $p$-th power on the $j$-finite chart: it is the Frobenius substitution $q \mapsto q^p$ on $q$-expansions, read through the model's function-field identification. It is used to derive the corresponding statement on places, [`ModularCurve.XHDRLevel.placeOfPoint_inv_efib_comp_eq_qExpFrobeniusPlaceModL_of_chart_pow`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRLevel.placeOfPoint_inv_efib_comp_eq_qExpFrobeniusPlaceModL_of_chart_pow), in the Deligne–Rapoport description of modular curves in characteristic $p$.
